## Routes (all verified 200)

- `/` Today · `/prelims` · `/mains` · `/gs-1`…`/gs-4` (rewrite → `/gs/:paper`)
- `/sources` · `/sources/[slug]` · `/daily` · `/daily/[y]/[m]/[d]` · `/saved`
- `/api/feeds/[sourceId]` — live RSS JSON preview

## Responsive layout

- **Mobile:** bottom tabs (Today, Sources, GS, Saved)
- **iPad/Desktop:** top pill nav + left sidebar
- **Touch:** 44px tap targets; dark mode via `prefers-color-scheme`

## Key source URL fixes (do not revert)

| Source | Use | Avoid |
|--------|-----|-------|
| Supreme Court | `https://www.sci.gov.in/press-release/` | `main.sci.gov.in` (dead) |
| ISRO | `https://www.isro.gov.in` | bare `isro.gov.in` |
| BRICS | MEA press releases URL | `brics2026.gov.in` (403) |
| PIB | `https://www.pib.gov.in` | generic homepage-only links |

**No open REST APIs** for Indian gov sources — only websites and occasional RSS. [public-apis](https://github.com/public-apis/public-apis) does not cover `.gov.in` UPSC sources.

**Working RSS:** DTE `stories.rss`, UN news RSS. PIB RSS endpoint exists but often returns empty items.

## Article card UX (implemented)

- Tap title → expand with 500ms animation
- Show 10 lines, then "Read more" (+10 lines per click)
- "Open original ↗" always visible with verified permalink
- Articles have `content[]` paragraphs for in-app reading

## Project structure

```
src/
├── app/           pages + /api/feeds/[sourceId]
├── components/    ArticleCard, SourceCard, layout nav, feeds
├── data/          sources.ts (15 sources), articles.ts (mock + helpers)
├── context/       SavedProvider (localStorage key: upsc-desk-saved)
├── lib/           feeds.ts (rss-parser), content.ts (line chunks), utils.ts
└── types/         Article, Source, GSPaper, Lens, SourceGroup
```

## Conventions

- **Always verify URLs with `curl` before adding** — run `bash scripts/verify-links.sh` after changing `articles.ts` or `sources.ts`
- GS routes: folder `src/app/gs/[paper]/page.tsx` + rewrite in `next.config.mjs`
- Source registry in `src/data/sources.ts` — add `rssFeedUrl` and `feedNote` when known
- Keep scope minimal; match existing Tailwind CSS variable theming in `globals.css`
- Single-user private app — no public signup, no coaching-site patterns

## User preferences (from prior chat)

- Both Prelims and Mains lenses
- iPad / mobile / desktop friendly
- Expandable in-app reading before opening original
- All article links must be verified working — audit with curl before adding
- Separate standalone repo only

